Task: Implement (Green) - GET /health and GET /health/ready endpoints

Summary:
Added OrderStore[F].ping: F[Boolean] to both backends - in-memory always true;
Postgres runs a trivial `SELECT 1` (via a Void-parameter skunk.Query, no
.prepare needed), timed like the other operations, with an outer .attempt so
an unreachable database yields false instead of propagating an error.

New HealthRoutes module: GET /health always returns 200 (serverLogicSuccess,
no real check); GET /health/ready returns 200 if store.ping is true, 503
(no body) otherwise. Wired into Main's Docs.routes list alongside the order
endpoints, so both are visible in Swagger too.

New HealthRoutesSuite (written in the prior Red task) covers all three cases
against stub OrderStore instances. Also added Postgres-level ping tests
(reachable -> true, unreachable via a bad port -> false) to
OrderStorePostgresSuite for parity with the other OrderStore methods.

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/orderservice/HealthRoutes.scala (new)
- src/main/scala/orderservice/{Main,OrderStore}.scala
- src/test/scala/orderservice/{OrderRoutesSuite,OrderStorePostgresSuite}.scala

Why: Implements this track's FR6 standard production-quality health endpoints
requirement (spec.md).

Verification: sbt scalafmtCheck Test/scalafmtCheck test - 49/49 pass.
